# Pins the otherwise-mutable v1.38.0 tag: a moved/re-cut tag fails the build
# instead of silently baking a swapped source. [Vuln-11]
#
# NOTE which artefact this hashes. telegraf is a Go package, so buildroot sets
# DOWNLOAD_POST_PROCESS = go (package/pkg-golang.mk): it fetches the upstream
# archive, vendors the module graph into it and REPACKS. The hash below is of
# that POST-PROCESSED archive — the only one buildroot ever verifies. The hash
# of the raw GitHub archive is a different value and makes every build fail
# (rc36 train, 2026-07-28).
#
# The upstream input was verified independently from two hosts before trusting
# the post-processed result:
#   curl -sL https://github.com/influxdata/telegraf/archive/refs/tags/v1.38.0.tar.gz | sha256sum
#     -> 18e3d7ba0a8e8ac1c8e8b619a5d97a704cfc9ea3cb49903d3894f0259e2f4a1a  (5167359 bytes)
#
# To recompute when bumping: verify the upstream archive hash as above FIRST,
# then run a bake and read the "got:" value buildroot reports. Deriving it from
# a failing build is only safe because the upstream input was checked first.
sha256  c1d79c22cf179799c348787107fea1f18e4e90669f960b1099580946feeda170  v1.38.0.tar.gz
sha256  c435b0efb886c4b05a62c4416aba91c93e481ccf62828fa61ae04bdaa9ea0813  LICENSE
